From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KL7 <kl7@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kl7: match AppleCLCD to the KL7 display node

The KL7 ADT describes /arm-io/disp0 as tecno,kl7-display, but AppleCLCD
only matched sweet,display.  As a result the display driver never probed,
no IOMobileFramebuffer service was published, and SpringBoard/backboardd
had no framebuffer to open.  Match the KL7 display-subsystem node so the
existing SweetFramebuffer implementation registers IOMobileFramebuffer.

This deliberately does not match kl7-fbcon (tecno,kl7-framebuffer): that
root node is the early-console carrier, not a second display provider.
---
 iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
     "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = AppleCLCD;"
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformDevice;"
-    "     'IONameMatch'     = 'sweet,display';"
+    "     'IONameMatch'     = ('sweet,display', 'tecno,kl7-display');"
     "   },"
     "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = SweetHIDButtons;"
